{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"6070129d-41e8-426e-81c9-31db76825c4c","status":"SUCCESS","response":"{\n  \"doc_id\": \"keepass\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-001\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_actor\",\n      \"evidence\": \"KeePass must be downloaded and installed\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Uses passive voice without specifying who performs the download and installation (e.g., end user or administrator), and omits the download source, version, target platform, and triggering precondition.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-003\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"referential\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Folder selected must be of type the database can read and that is “name”.kdb\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"The demonstrative 'that' has multiple plausible antecedents ('Folder selected', 'type', or 'database'), and conflating 'Folder' with the file pattern '“name”.kdb' makes it unclear whether a directory or a .kdb file is selected.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-003\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_error_handling\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Folder selected must be of type the database can read and that is “name”.kdb\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Specifies a file/type validation rule on the happy path without stating what happens when an unsupported or unreadable file/folder is selected, and omits the actor who selects it.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-004\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"syntactic\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Databases must have different names or else the previews one will be replace if selected\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"The conditional clause 'if selected' is syntactically ambiguous as to whether the existing database is overwritten automatically when a duplicate name is chosen or only if the user explicitly confirms an overwrite prompt, and 'the previews one' has an unclear scope.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-004\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_condition\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Databases must have different names or else the previews one will be replace if selected\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Omits the scope boundary for name uniqueness (same directory vs. entire system), omits the actor performing the selection and replacement, and does not specify whether a warning or confirmation prompt precedes overwriting.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-005\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_actor\",\n      \"evidence\": \"There must be entries in the database in order for them to be printed\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Uses passive voice ('to be printed') without specifying which actor or component initiates printing, and omits what happens if printing is attempted on an empty database.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-006\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"vague_term\",\n      \"evidence\": \"All data related to the word must be shown\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"'All data related to the word' is vague and lacks testable matching criteria, leaving unspecified which fields are searched, whether matching is case-sensitive or substring-based, and whether full entry data (including plaintext passwords) is displayed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-006\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_error_handling\",\n      \"evidence\": \"All data related to the word must be shown\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Describes a search lookup on the happy path without specifying system behavior when no entries match the search term or when the input is empty, and uses passive voice ('must be shown') without naming the responsible system component.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-007\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_error_handling\",\n      \"evidence\": \"A name is required in order for the new group/subgroup to be created\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Specifies a required-field validation without stating what happens if the name is missing or invalid (e.g., error message or disabled creation), omits valid-name rules, and uses passive voice ('to be created') without naming the actor.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-008\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_error_handling\",\n      \"evidence\": \"A subgroup cannot be created when no group is selected\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"States a precondition restriction without specifying how the system handles an attempt to create a subgroup with no group selected (e.g., disabling the action or displaying an error), and uses passive voice without identifying the actor.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-009\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_error_handling\",\n      \"evidence\": \"A name is required in order for the group/subgroup to be renamed\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Specifies a required-field validation without stating system behavior when an empty or invalid name is submitted, omits name constraints, and uses passive voice ('to be renamed') without naming the actor.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-010\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"vague_term\",\n      \"evidence\": \"find something in a group a word must be placed in the find field\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"'something' does not specify what entities or fields are searchable, and 'a word' is imprecise as to whether partial strings, numbers, symbols, or multi-word queries are permitted.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-010\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_error_handling\",\n      \"evidence\": \"In order to find something in a group a word must be placed in the find field\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Describes a search precondition without specifying what happens when the find field is empty or no matches are found, and uses passive voice ('must be placed') without naming the actor.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-011\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"syntactic\",\n      \"evidence\": \"An entry must belong to a group to be created\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Syntactically ambiguous between requiring an entry to belong to an existing group in order for the entry to be created versus belonging to a group that is yet to be created; also unclear whether 'a group' includes subgroups.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-011\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_error_handling\",\n      \"evidence\": \"An entry must belong to a group to be created\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Does not specify what happens if a user attempts to create an entry without selecting or assigning a group (e.g., error prompt, disabled action, or default group), and uses passive voice ('to be created') without naming the actor.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-012\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_error_handling\",\n      \"evidence\": \"When the password field is completed the repeat password field must be completed\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"States a field-validation rule without specifying what happens if the repeat password field is not completed, omits the scope (master password vs. entry password), and uses passive voice without naming the actor.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-013\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_error_handling\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Password field and repeat password field must be identical\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"States a validation requirement without specifying system behavior when the two password fields do not match (e.g., blocking save and displaying an error), and omits whether this applies to master passwords, entry passwords, or both.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-014\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_error_handling\",\n      \"evidence\": \"An entry must be selected to be viewed or modified\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"States a precondition without specifying system behavior if viewing or modifying is attempted when no entry is selected (e.g., disabling actions or showing a prompt), and uses passive voice without naming the actor.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-015\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_error_handling\",\n      \"evidence\": \"When the password field is changed the repeat password field must be Changed and be identical with password field\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Does not specify what happens if the repeat password field is not updated or does not match the modified password field, omits the scope (master vs. entry password), and uses passive voice without naming the actor.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-015\",\n      \"type\": \"inconsistency\",\n      \"subtype\": \"duplicate\",\n      \"evidence\": \"When the password field is changed the repeat password field must be Changed and be identical with password field\",\n      \"related_ids\": [\n        \"KP-012\",\n        \"KP-013\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"Repeats the unconditional identical-password validation already stated in KP-013 and largely duplicates the repeat-password completion rule in KP-012 without defining a distinct scope.\"