y policy, or delay), does not state that the entered password must be correct, and omits the user actor.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-024\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"vague_term\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unless the key file is present\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"'present' is vague and does not define where the key file must reside (e.g., user-specified path, default directory, or removable media) or whether file validity and readability are required.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-024\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_error_handling\",\n      \"evidence\": \"If a key file is required to unlock the database, the database doesn’t open unless the key file is present\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Describes an authentication check without specifying system behavior when the key file is missing, unreadable, corrupted, or invalid (e.g., error message or retry prompt).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-025\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_error_handling\",\n      \"evidence\": \"If there is a composite key, both master password and key file are required\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Describes a composite authentication requirement without specifying system behavior when only one credential is provided or when either credential is invalid, and omits the target operation (unlocking the database).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-028\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"vague_term\",\n      \"evidence\": \"File formats are not specialized password database formats\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"'File formats' and 'specialized password database formats' are vague and undefined, leaving unclear which formats are covered and what criteria distinguish a specialized password database format.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": 